//The second line contains n space-separated integers, representing the array elements.

Constraints

NA

Output Format

Print "Yes" if the array is a palindrome.

Print "No" otherwise.

Sample Input 0

5
1 2 3 2 1
Sample Output 0

Yes
Explanation 0

The array reads the same forward and backward: 1 2 3 2 1.

Sample Input 1

4
1 2 3 4
Sample Output 1

No
Explanation 1

The array reads 1 2 3 4 forward and 4 3 2 1 backward, which are not the same.//
import java.util.*;
public class main
{
    public static void main(String args[]){
    Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);
    int n=sc.nextInt();
    int arr[]=new int[n];
    for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
    {
        arr[i]=sc.nextInt();
    }
    int l=0;
    int r=n-1;
    while(l<r){
    if (arr[l]!=arr[r]){
        System.out.print("No");
        return;
    }
    l++;
    r--;
    }
    System.out.print("Yes");
}
}

